course: dictionary
lesson: 12522
title: Choosing and marking with designate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Designate is a formal word with a clear core idea: to choose someone or something officially for a job or purpose. When you designate something, you make the choice official. «The school designated the back field as a play zone.» The clue is "as a play zone": the field now has a special purpose.
explain: Look at the words around designate. It often comes with "as" or "for": designate someone as captain, or designate an area for games. «The teacher designated Mia as team captain.» The sentence tells you the teacher chose Mia for a job, so designate means chose officially.
explain: Designated can also come before a noun, as an adjective. «The designated driver stayed sober so everyone got home safely.» The designated driver is the person chosen for that job. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "chosen" in its place to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Designate means to choose someone or something officially for a job or purpose.
fact: Designate also means to mark or name something in a special way.
fact: «Designated» can describe a noun: «the designated area» is an area chosen for a special use.
fact: «President-designate» means someone chosen for the job of president but not started yet.
fact: In maths, «let x designate the number» means x is the name we give to that number.
exercise: «The school designated the back field as a play zone.» What does designated mean here? | Closed for the winter | *Chosen for a special purpose | Painted green | Lost and forgotten
exercise: «Ravi was the designated driver, so he drove everyone home safely.» What is a designated driver? | A car made in the same year | A person who drives very fast | A person who lives on the same street | *A person chosen to stay sober and drive
exercise: «The president-designate will start her job next month.» What does president-designate mean? | *Chosen to be president, but not started yet | A president who is very tall | A president who everyone loves | A president who has retired
test: Which word means to choose something officially for a purpose? | *Designate | Ignore | Wander | Giggle
test: «The teacher designated Jake to hand out the books.» Who was given the job? | Nobody, because it was not decided | The books | *Jake | The teacher
exam: Which sentence uses designate correctly? | The bike designates lunch for the rain. | *The sign designates this road as a bike lane. | I designate my sandwich to be a bike. | The road designates a sad feeling today.
